{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G4CfZ62MZRoLJWDDtySNLz","type":"tool_result","content":"# Farmers Markets Summary\n\nBased on the provided data, I summed the `farmers_markets` column for all 50 U.S. states plus Washington, D.C., excluding the territories (Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands).\n\n**Grand Total: 10,046 farmers markets**\n\nThis figure represents the combined count of farmers markets across the continental United States and the District of Columbia. California leads with 647 markets, followed by New York with 555 and Pennsylvania with 426."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aaa3d9c6-a26e-45b7-b98d-ee5ff9587783","uuid":"629d64fd-977f-4146-a528-02e5ea156992","timestamp":"2026-08-16T20:07:17.917Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":2651,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Farmers Markets Summary\n\nBased on the provided data, I summed the `farmers_markets` column for all 50 U.S. states plus Washington, D.C., excluding the territories (Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands).\n\n**Grand Total: 10,046 farmers markets**\n\nThis figure represents the combined count of farmers markets across the continental United States and the District of Columbia. California leads with 647 markets, followed by New York with 555 and Pennsylvania with 426.","durationMs":1995,"url":"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv"}}
